Report #137/#138 (recurring "missing reagent" from the reagent bank): the
craft refusal path in Spell::CheckItems shipped with ZERO instrumentation,
which is why four "fixes" could not be diagnosed -- a silent early-return
leaves nothing in Server.log to read. Per the 0.1.104/0.1.105 sweep lesson,
this module's diagnostic counters are LOG_INFO so they reach Server.log at
the live Logger.module level.

When a craft is refused with SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS and the vault was
consulted, the log now names the spell id, the reagent id and count, the
bags+bank stock, and the vault stock. A genuine shortfall vs a stale client
is then distinguishable from the log alone.

Additions:
- LivingGearVault::VaultCount exposed as LivingGear_VaultCountForDiag()
  (read-only) and forward-declared in Spell.cpp next to the existing
  LivingGear vault prototypes.
- Refusal site in Spell::CheckItems (the SPELL_FAILED_REAGENTS return in
  the Reagent[] loop, ~line 7474) logs
  "reagent bank craft refused: spell N wants ITEM xN, bags+bank N, vault N"
  before returning.

No behavior change: the gate, the answer, and the return value are identical;
only the log line is new.
